    "summary": "Model built and passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nBridge: single simply supported span, 30 m bearing-centre to bearing-centre, deck width 10 m, carriageway 9 m, two-way traffic, Highway Class II (JTG D60-2015), two design lanes. Structure idealized as a spine_beam_2d with a \"simply_supported\" system.\n\nGirders: 3 precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C40, prestressed concrete), combined into one spine beam per MR-02: single midspan section A = 1.13893 m², I = 0.35492 m⁴; combined girder.A = 3.41679 m² and girder.I = 1.06475 m⁴. γ = 26.0 kN/m³ (JTGD60-4.2.1), so w = 88.836 kN/m and m = 9.0557 t/m (MR-07). Ec = 32500 MPa.\n\nBearings/boundary: plain laminated elastomeric bearings at both abutments, 2 per girder end (6 per support line), 300×400 mm effective plan, 5 internal layers × 8 mm. Shape factor S = 10.714; from JTG 3362-2018 8.7: Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m per support line; vertical/longitudinal springs with free rotation.\n\nLive load: Class II, two lanes, ξ = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, impact factor μ = 0.2006 from f1 = 3.402 Hz (JTGD60-4.3.2).\n\nKey results: first three vertical frequencies 3.40 / 13.49 / 29.88 Hz; total self weight 2665.1 kN (reactions 1332.5 kN per abutment); self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m; governing live-load moment 6449.6 kN·m at midspan.\n\nRepair made: the initially accepted girder.A was the SINGLE-girder area (1.1389 m²), inconsistent with MR-02 (which requires A_single × n_girders for the merged spine beam) and with girder.w = γ·A_combined. This made the L2-1 parameter recomputation and the L3-2 total-weight check (γ × A × L) fail. Correcting girder.A to 3.41679 m² (n=3) and re-affirming the dependent girder.I, girder.w and girder.m resolved both failures; the regenerated model passes."
